ll regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was healthy only in staging, so it was not used.) After the rollback, all regions are running v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before deploying it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15617, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01H53tXNEace11PotwQMTBBX", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15617, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01H53tXNEace11PotwQMTBBX", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19014, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again.\n\n- **Problem:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was newer, but it was only ever healthy in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **Result:** All three regions are now on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api describing the failure, the rollback and the current status, and the on-call engineer was paged. It also notes that someone needs to find out why v2.3.1 failed before it's deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01REvEA5KCoTUdJFCEKCGACt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "tool