{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again.\n\n- **Problem:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was newer, but it was only ever healthy in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **Result:** All three regions are now on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, and the error rate is down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api describing the failure, the rollback and the current status, and the on-call engineer was paged. It also notes that someone needs to find out why v2.3.1 failed before it's deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}